Module 6 — Live Tracking, ETA & Cascading Fallback
Complete End-to-End Technical Documentation
The Live Tracking, ETA & Cascading Fallback Module is responsible for two closely connected requirements of UyirKappan:
1.	Continuously monitoring the assigned ambulance and communicating its current status/ETA to stakeholders.
2.	Ensuring that an emergency request does not remain unattended when an assigned ambulance rejects or fails to respond.
The module connects the Driver Application, Backend, Bystander Application, Hospital Dashboard, and Intelligent Dispatch Engine into one continuous response workflow.
The first-review architecture already identifies live location updates from the driver, backend-mediated real-time communication, ETA updates to the bystander and hospital, and cascading fallback when an assigned ambulance rejects or times out.
________________________________________
1. Purpose of the Module
The module's primary objective is:
Maintain continuous visibility of an active emergency response while automatically recovering from failed ambulance assignments.
The complete flow is:
Ambulance Assigned
       ↓
Driver Accepts
       ↓
Live Location Tracking
       ↓
ETA Calculation
       ↓
Bystander + Hospital Updates
       ↓
Ambulance Movement
       ↓
ETA Recalculation
       ↓
Patient Arrival
       ↓
Hospital Journey
       ↓
Completion
If the driver does not accept:
Ambulance Assigned
       ↓
Reject / Timeout
       ↓
Cascading Fallback
       ↓
Dispatch Engine Re-run
       ↓
Next Best Ambulance
       ↓
Driver Assignment
