40. Final Definition of Module 6
Live Tracking, ETA & Cascading Fallback
The Live Tracking, ETA & Cascading Fallback module provides continuous visibility and resilience throughout the UyirKappan emergency-response lifecycle. After an ambulance accepts an assignment, its simulated/real location is continuously transmitted to the backend and propagated to the bystander application and hospital dashboard through real-time communication. The system continuously recalculates the ambulance's expected arrival time based on its current position, remaining route, and simulated traffic conditions, allowing ETA and route information to change dynamically. In parallel, the cascading fallback mechanism monitors ambulance assignment responses and automatically triggers re-dispatch when a selected ambulance rejects or fails to respond within a configurable timeout. The failed ambulance is recorded and excluded from subsequent attempts, after which the Intelligent Dispatch Engine is invoked again to identify the next suitable candidate. The process continues until an ambulance accepts or no suitable candidates remain. The initial implementation will reproduce these behaviors using simulated ambulance movement, virtual traffic, configurable driver responses, and controlled emergency scenarios, generating measurable data for response-time, fallback, ETA, and reliability evaluation.
Core implementation pipeline
Assignment
    ↓
Driver Response
    ↓
 ┌───────────────┐
 │               │
ACCEPT       REJECT/TIMEOUT
 │               │
 ▼               ▼
Tracking       Fallback
 │               │
 ▼               ▼
ETA          Re-run Dispatch
 │               │
 ▼               ▼
Bystander    Next Ambulance
 │               │
 ▼               ▼
Hospital       Accept
 │               │
 └───────┬───────┘
         ▼
   Live Tracking
         ↓
    Dynamic ETA
         ↓
   Patient Arrival
         ↓
  Hospital Arrival
         ↓
      Complete
This module is effectively the "response continuity" layer of UyirKappan: the Intelligent Dispatch Engine decides who should respond, while this module ensures that the response continues to be monitored and that a failed assignment automatically transitions to the next suitable ambulance.

